<title>GREECE: ASPIS MUTUAL FUNDS SAYS ASSETS UP 20 PCT IN JAN.</title>
<headline>ASPIS MUTUAL FUNDS SAYS ASSETS UP 20 PCT IN JAN.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aspis Mutual Funds assets rose more than 20 percent in January reaching 35 billion drachmas, it said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>In 1996, Aspis income fund had a net return of 15.27 percent, with the average annual T-bill rate at 12.8 percent and the average annual savings deposit interest rate at 10.2 percent.</p>
<p>The Aspis Group comprises ten companies engaged in investment, banking, insurance and stock broking activities. It employs 1,400 people. --Margarita Sotiropoulou, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
